- **Runtime execution:** Native machine code runs directly on the CPU. There is no per-statement translation overhead at runtime, so execution speed is determined by the algorithm’s complexity, not by the language implementation.
- **Space complexity:**  
  - *Disk:* The executable binary occupies storage space.  
  - *RAM:* Only the compiled program and its data reside in memory; the compiler itself is not needed at runtime.  
